---
title: "Air Conditioning"
code: "AIR-176"
category: "a-c-and-refrigeration"
credits: "6"
prerequisites: []
corequisites:
  - "2026/AIR-134"
corequisiteNote: "Corequisite: AIR 134"
---

Presents residential and commercial air conditioning systems, including air conditioning principles, psychometrics and pressure balancing. Includes window units, residential central systems, small commercial (air- and water-cooled condensers) and automobile units. Lecture 4 hours. Laboratory 4 hours, Total 8 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
